# Optional. Nothing here is required: without it the workspace keeps everything in the browser.
# Make this app the workspace's backend (see "Built-in home-server API" in docs/backend-api.md).
NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKSPACE_API_URL=/api/workspace

# Where the server keeps workspace data (one JSON file per resource). Default: ./.logio-data
LOGIO_DATA_DIR=/srv/logio-data

# Where skills delivered to an agent are written: <dir>/<agent id>/<skill>/SKILL.md. Default: <LOGIO_DATA_DIR>/agents
LOGIO_AGENT_SKILLS_DIR=/srv/agent-skills

# Only these agent ids may receive skills (comma separated). Unset allows any well-formed id.
# LOGIO_AGENTS=research-agent,coder

# Without a token the API answers only on localhost / private network names. Set a long random token to expose it
# beyond your LAN; every request must then send "Authorization: Bearer <token>" (window.__workspaceBackendConfig.headers).
# LOGIO_API_TOKEN=
# LOGIO_ALLOWED_HOSTS=nas.example.net
